cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "IAE-SLMS: Small Language Models — Applications, Fine-Tuning & Deployment"
message: "If you use this research, datasets, or any part of this repository, please cite it as below."
type: software
abstract: >-
  Five task-specific studies on adapting small language models (270M–8B parameters)
  using parameter-efficient fine-tuning (LoRA/QLoRA) for production NLP tasks.
  Covers multilingual sentiment classification across English, Arabic, Urdu, and
  Roman Urdu (120K-sample curated dataset); chain-of-thought reasoning induction
  via supervised fine-tuning; length-controlled abstractive summarization with
  epoch-wise hallucination analysis; the first fine-tuned conversational AI for
  Roman Urdu (a low-resource language with 70M+ speakers); and retrieval-augmented
  generation with perfect retrieval precision. All experiments run on free-tier
  Google Colab GPUs using 4-bit NF4 quantization, achieving 74% GPU memory
  reduction via QLoRA. Deployment benchmarked on CPU (llama.cpp) and GPU (vLLM).
authors:
  - name: "IAE SLMS Research Team"
keywords:
  - small language models
  - parameter-efficient fine-tuning
  - LoRA
  - QLoRA
